es a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [156 4 "// a view of a view: the same buffer, start, length and stride (CPython's memory_from_buffer keeps the"] [157 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [163 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [177 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [187 2 "// memory_hash (queue 249): a read-only byte view's hash is its bytes' (hash(b'..')), the exporter hashed first with"] [188 2 "// the view exported meanwhile (gh-142664: a re-entrant __hash__ that releases the view gets BufferError)"] [260 2 "// item and slice assignment into a writable buffer (PY6d's REQUEST: _pyio's readinto, pickle's protocol 5"] [261 2 "// bytearray); byte views only"] [395 4 "// a view of the same memory (writable through a bytearray's)"] [402 20 "// the same memory, so a writable view stays writable (PY6d's REQUEST)"] [415 2 "// count, index and toreadonly (PY7: absent): over tolist's items, as memory_count and memory_index"] [485 3 "// a 1-D view's shape, strides and contiguity (PY7: absent)"] [503 34 "// CHECK_RELEASED (PY7: obj stayed readable; no attribute \"released\", CPython's has none)"] [511 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [512 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."] [523 1 "// isReadonly is view->readonly: a toreadonly's or __buffer__'s view, or one of an exporter that is not writable (queue 249:"] [524 1 "// an array's buffer is writable, as arraymodule.c exports it; only a bytearray's was before)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[53 47] [69 55] [89 17] [91 16] [111 17] [111 25] [129 24] [134 24] [134 33] [155 33] [163 35] [164 24] [169 37] [194 25] [200 19] [203 26] [230 25] [237 25] [240 26] [264 25] [284 26] [297 14] [297 21] [343 40]